From 8d5638860612c63eb40a46e6bbb404ddaacb1e2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:52:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings: the Spanish files of Estuary lose the obsolete
 entries of ids that they also have as active ones

es_es, es_ar and es_mx kept, from before, 10, 7 and 10 entries marked obsolete ("#~") of an id
that also has an active entry: 31025, 31112, 31115, 31137, 31138, 31149 and 31612 to 31615.
They were the translations of other texts that upstream gave those ids (or of the older text of
31025), which no parser reads and which a reader could take for the translation of the active
text. The active entry of each stays as it is (the msgid of every one is the one of en_gb;
none of the obsolete ones had the same msgid with a translation that the active one lacks).
---
 .../resource.language.es_ar/strings.po        | 28 -------------
 .../resource.language.es_es/strings.po        | 40 -------------------
 .../resource.language.es_mx/strings.po        | 40 -------------------
 3 files changed, 108 deletions(-)

